e or support.\n\nAlso, my hand has limited high-value combinations. Playing the A-high straight uses up key high cards (A, K, Q, J, 10), leaving me with lower-mid cards like 8s, 6, 5s, 4s, and two 2s. If the landlord still has bombs or rockets, that could be risky.\n\nMoreover, card counting shows: A:1, K:1, Q:1, 10:1 — these are all accounted for in my hand or played. Since I hold ♥A, ♣A, ♦K, ♥Q, ♦10 — and only one A and K remain unaccounted (but I have both Aces? Wait: original deck has 4 Aces. Played: ♦A by landlord earlier. My hand: ♥A, ♣A. So two Aces left unknown? But count says A:1 — so one Ace unaccounted. Similarly, K:1 — I have ♦K, three played: ♠K, ? — need to reconcile.\n\nBut per given "Cards Remaining Unknown", we trust the count: A:1, K:1, Q:1, 10:1 — meaning I must not hold duplicates beyond what\'s allowed. Wait — my hand: ♥A, ♣A — that\'s two Aces. But "A:1" implies only one Ace remains unknown — contradiction?\n\nWait: "Cards Remaining Unknown" means cards not yet seen — i.e., not played and not in my hand. So the count is about hidden cards. So:\n\nTotal Aces: 4  \nPlayed: ♦A (by landlord Turn 1)  \nMy hand: ♥A, ♣A → so three accounted  \nThus one Ace still unknown → matches "A:1"\n\nSimilarly, K: I have ♦K, played: ♠K → so two accounted, two total unaccounted? But count says K:1 — wait no: original four Kings.\n\nPlayed: ♠K  \nMy hand: ♦K  \nSo two known, thus 2 unknown — but count says K:1 → inconsistency?\n\nWait, perhaps the count reflects remaining in the game: unseen cards among opponent and undealt? But in standard 3-player Dou Dizhu, 51 cards dealt (17 each), 3 leftover. But here, some cards played.\n\nActually, the "Cards Remaining Unknown" likely refers to cards not in my hand and not seen in play — so yes, it should be consistent.\n\nGiven: My hand has ♥A, ♣A → two Aces  \nPlayed: ♦A → one  \nSo three seen → one Ace missing → "A:1" correct\n\nKing: I have ♦K  \nPlayed: ♠K  \nSo two seen → two unknown → but count says K:1 → discrepancy.